// RX Monitor sample rate: SvxLink's QSO Recorder writes audio at its own
// internal processing rate, not the sound card's rate (CARD_SAMPLE_RATE=
// 48000 in svxlink.conf is unrelated -- that's ALSA I/O, SvxLink resamples
// to its internal rate before this ever reaches a file). Confirmed via
// `file` on an actual recorded .mp3: "16 kHz, Monaural". The player used to
// assume 48000 (32000 on iOS) instead, and the "resample" branch below meant
// to reconcile that was itself broken (read `this.sampleRate` off the
// WebSocket object, which doesn't have that property, so the branch
// referencing the *intended* source rate never ran) -- net effect, 16kHz
// audio got played back through a 48kHz-configured buffer, 3x too fast and
// pitched way up. Not silence exactly, but distorted enough that a short
// transmission could easily read as "I hear nothing." Fixed 2026-09-07: feed
// PCMPlayer at the real 16000 rate on every platform and feed it every
// incoming chunk directly -- no resampling needed once the rates actually
// match.
